              "title": "Source E (Written Extract): Roger Bacon, Opus Majus, on Authority and Experience (c.1267)",
              "text": "There are four chief obstacles to grasping the truth: the example of frail and unworthy authority, long-established custom, the sense of the ignorant crowd, and the hiding of one’s own ignorance under the show of wisdom. Reasoning draws a conclusion, but it does not make the conclusion certain unless the mind discovers it by the path of experience. If a man who had never seen fire were proved by satisfactory arguments that fire burns, his mind would not be satisfied until he had placed his hand into the flame.",
