          "act": 4,
          "act_title": "Stage 4: Herbal Apothecary Remedies & Theriac — Why did herbal recipes remain popular across all social classes?",
          "theme": "Herbal Pharmacy: Simples, Electuaries, and Theriac",
          "title": "Herbal Pharmacy: Simples, Electuaries, and Theriac",
          "content": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[4.1]</span> Herbal pharmacy provided the vast majority of everyday remedies. Apothecaries and local wise women brewed herbal potions prepared as single herbs (**simples**) or complex sweetened compounds (**electuaries**).<br><br><span class=\"para-ref\">[4.2]</span> Common ingredients included mint for digestion, willow bark for fever pain, and honey as an antiseptic dressing. The most prestigious medicine was **Theriac** (Venice Treacle), an ancient compound containing over sixty ingredients including snake flesh and opium. Believed to purge poisons from the heart, Theriac was prescribed for everything from snakebites to epidemic fevers.",
          "text": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[4.1]</span> Herbal pharmacy provided the vast majority of everyday remedies. Apothecaries and local wise women brewed herbal potions prepared as single herbs (**simples**) or complex sweetened compounds (**electuaries**).<br><br><span class=\"para-ref\">[4.2]</span> Common ingredients included mint for digestion, willow bark for fever pain, and honey as an antiseptic dressing. The most prestigious medicine was **Theriac** (Venice Treacle), an ancient compound containing over sixty ingredients including snake flesh and opium. Believed to purge poisons from the heart, Theriac was prescribed for everything from snakebites to epidemic fevers.",
