          "content": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[3.1]</span> Lacking knowledge of bacteria, medieval society explained the Black Death through religious, astrological, and environmental frameworks. Most believed the plague was **God's punishment** for human wickedness, swearing, and sinful pride.<br><br><span class=\"para-ref\">[3.2]</span> Astrologers pointed to a catastrophic alignment of planets in 1345, claiming the conjunction of Saturn, Jupiter, and Mars in Aquarius corrupted atmospheric air. Physicians blamed foul **miasma** released by earthquakes and unburied dead bodies, arguing corrupt air entered pores and poisoned the blood.",
