          "content": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[4.1]</span> In 1665, the Royal Society’s secretary, Henry Oldenburg, founded *Philosophical Transactions*, the world’s first scientific academic journal (<span class=\"archival-meta-tag\">Source A</span>).<br><br><span class=\"para-ref\">[4.2]</span> The journal established the modern standard of **scientific peer review**, publishing letters, dissection reports, and microscope observations from researchers across Europe. This enabled scientists like William Harvey, Robert Hooke, and Antoni van Leeuwenhoek to share findings rapidly, creating an international scientific community committed to experimental progress.",
