              "model_answer": "Source A shows that Sydenham published his detailed clinical case histories in Latin under the title Observationes Medicae ('Medical Observations'), demonstrating that he sought to persuade the wider medical profession to adopt systematic bedside recording of acute disease symptoms rather than relying on ancient Galenic theory.",
