          "text": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[4.1]</span> Sydenham championed treatments proven by practical results rather than humoral theory. He popularized the medical use of **Peruvian Bark** (Cinchona bark / Jesuit's bark), recognizing that it cured malarial fevers (*agues*).<br><br><span class=\"para-ref\">[4.2]</span> Because Cinchona did not purge humours, traditional Galenists had rejected it; Sydenham proved its clinical efficacy (later discovered to contain quinine). He also created liquid **laudanum** (purified opium in alcohol), providing reliable pain relief and establishing modern clinical pharmacology.",
