          "theme": "The Limits of Sydenham’s Legacy",
          "content": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[5.1]</span> Despite his observational brilliance, Sydenham remained constrained by seventeenth-century knowledge. He still believed disease was influenced by atmospheric **miasma** and seasonal climate, having no concept of microscopic bacteria.<br><br><span class=\"para-ref\">[5.2]</span> Nevertheless, his empirical methodology was monumental: by insisting that clinical observation at the bedside must triumph over ancient written dogma, Sydenham laid the practical foundations of modern evidence-based clinical medicine.",
