              "letter": "E",
              "type": "written",
              "title": "Source E (Written Extract): Jacobus Sylvius, Vindication of Galen Against the Madman Vesalius (1551)",
              "text": "I implore his Imperial Majesty to severely punish this monster of insolence, Andreas Vesalius, who with slanderous tongue and impious hands striveth to destroy the immortal work of Galen! If the human body today differs in any part from what Galen described, it is not Galen who was mistaken, but rather human nature which hath degenerated and altered its structure since classical antiquity. Galen remaineth the prince of physicians, whose sacred texts must not be touched by profane heretics.",
              "caption": "Extract from the pamphlet published by Parisian medical professor Jacobus Sylvius in 1551, fiercely attacking his former pupil Vesalius.",
              "desc": "Conservative defense of Galen claiming that if the human body differed from Galen's descriptions, human anatomy had degenerated since antiquity.",
