          "content": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[1.1]</span> English physician **William Harvey** (1578–1657) studied medicine at Padua under Hieronymus Fabricius, who discovered that human veins contained tiny one-way flaps (**valves**).<br><br><span class=\"para-ref\">[1.2]</span> Returning to London, Harvey dissected cold-blooded animals (frogs, snakes) whose slow heartbeats allowed him to observe muscle contractions. He realized the heart was not a furnace creating heat, but a mechanical muscular **pump** propelling blood through vessels.",
