          "content": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[2.1]</span> For 1,500 years, Galenic doctrine held that the liver continuously manufactured fresh venous blood from digested food, which was consumed by tissues as fuel.<br><br><span class=\"para-ref\">[2.2]</span> Harvey applied revolutionary mathematical calculations to disprove this: calculating that the heart pumped three times a human's body weight in blood every hour. It was biologically impossible for the liver to produce such immense volumes from food. Therefore, Harvey concluded blood must circulate continuously through a closed circulatory system.",
