          "content": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[3.1]</span> In 1628, Harvey published his findings in *De Motu Cordis* (*On the Motion of the Heart and Blood*). He proved his theory using elegant, repeatable **tourniquet experiments** on human arms (<span class=\"archival-meta-tag\">Source A</span>).<br><br><span class=\"para-ref\">[3.2]</span> Tying a tight tourniquet halted blood flow into the lower arm; loosening it slightly allowed arterial blood through, making veins swell below the bandage. Pushing blood along a vein with his finger proved valves only allowed blood toward the heart, demonstrating complete circulation.",
