          "title": "Source B (Written Extract): William Harvey, De Motu Cordis, Mathematical Proof of Blood Volume (1628)",
          "text": "Let us calculate the quantity of blood pumped by the heart. If the left ventricle contains two ounces of blood, and the pulse beats seventy times in a minute, the heart must expel over five hundred ounces of blood in an hour—which is thrice the weight of the entire human body! Whence can all this blood come? It is impossible that the liver could continuously manufacture such an enormous mass of blood from ingested food. Therefore, I was forced to conclude that blood is driven in a perpetual circle by the beat of the heart.",
