      "vocab_cloze_text": "During the 1665 epidemic, London parishes published weekly [Bills of Mortality] to monitor casualties. Parishes appointed [Searchers of the Dead] to inspect corpses for buboes. To contain the spread, the Mayor enforced strict [Municipal Quarantine], padlocking infected houses for 28 days with red crosses. Physicians wore a protective [Plague Doctor Beak] packed with dried herbs, while citizens carried a [Miasmatic Pomander] against foul air. At night, dead-carts dumped bodies into [Mass Lime Pits] outside the city walls. Yet because rat fleas were unknown, these civic efforts could not stop the epidemic.",
