              "citation": "Dr H. Charlton Bastian, Professor of Pathological Anatomy at University College London, The Lancet, March 1875.",
              "content": "We must not be misled by French and German laboratory experiments on vegetable infusions and beef teas into adopting extravagant germ dogmas. The living human body is entirely different from a sterile glass flask. In hundreds of clinical cases of epidemic fever, we observe chemical ferments arising spontaneously within diseased body fluids under conditions of foul atmospheric miasma and constitutional debility. To assert that every disease is produced by a distinct external parasite enters the realm of unscientific speculation.",
