          "source_context": "In 1842, social reformer Edwin Chadwick published his landmark sanitary survey, linking filth and poverty to epidemic diseases, leading directly to the Public Health Act 1848. **Hinge Question:** How did Edwin Chadwick use empirical evidence to convince parliament that sanitary reform was cheaper than supporting impoverished widows and orphans?",
