          "content": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[2.1]</span> Mid-twentieth-century diagnostics shifted from gross anatomy to cellular and biochemical testing. Automated blood analyses tested for anaemia, white blood cell counts (leukaemia), and hormonal imbalances, while glucose testing transformed diabetes care.<br><br><span class=\"para-ref\">[2.2]</span> In the 1950s and 1960s, **fibre-optic endoscopy** revolutionized internal medicine. Flexible glass bundles illuminated and transmitted live video from inside stomachs and intestines, allowing doctors to inspect ulcers and biopsy internal tumours without major abdominal surgery.",
