          "content": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[3.1]</span> While pharmaceuticals advanced, interwar British healthcare remained deeply unequal. Working men paid into National Insurance for GP care, but wives and children were uncovered; working-class families delayed calling doctors due to ruinous medical bills.<br><br><span class=\"para-ref\">[3.2]</span> In December 1942, during the dark days of the Second World War, economist Sir William Beveridge published the landmark **Beveridge Report**. He pledged to slay the \"Five Giants\" haunting society: Want, Ignorance, Squalor, Idleness, and **Disease**, proposing a comprehensive, state-funded National Health Service free at the point of delivery.",
