      "vocab_cloze_text": "In the early 1900s, Paul Ehrlich sought a [Magic Bullet] that could destroy specific bacteria without harming patient cells. In 1909, Sahachiro Hata tested hundreds of arsenic compounds to discover [Salvarsan 606], which cured syphilis. In 1932, Gerhard Domagk discovered [Prontosil], curing streptococcal infections. While science produced drugs, healthcare remained private until the 1942 [Beveridge Report] called for a war on Disease. On 5 July 1948, Minister of Health Aneurin Bevan overcame doctor opposition to launch the [National Health Service (NHS)], offering free healthcare funded by taxation to all citizens.",
