              "citation": "Wellcome Collection, London (RAMC Historical Records / Educational Use).",
              "content": "Beneath the ruined city of Arras lies a subterranean city carved out of ancient chalk quarries by the New Zealand Tunnelling Company. Here, thirty feet below ground, safe from the heaviest German artillery, the RAMC has established a fully equipped hospital known as Thompson's Cave. It contains 700 hospital beds arranged in long chalk galleries, fully fitted operating theatres with electric lighting, a mortuary, and piped water. Wounded men are brought directly from the battlefront through underground communication tunnels without ever coming into view of enemy observers or exposing stretcher bearers to shellfire.",
              "question_badge": "SUBTERRANEAN SURGERY: ARRAS UNDERGROUND HOSPITAL",
