              "model_answer": "The medical officer's purpose in Source D is to document how military engineers and the RAMC successfully adapted subterranean chalk geography to solve the mortal danger of surface artillery bombardment. By highlighting the 700 beds, electric lighting, and operating theatres thirty feet underground, the author intends to showcase the peak of logistical ingenuity: protecting wounded men and surgical teams from shellfire while ensuring emergency triage could proceed uninterrupted during the massive April 1917 Arras offensive.",
