              "hinge_question": "Why did high explosive artillery shrapnel create far more dangerous and infectious wounds than rifle bullets?",
              "source_context": "Artillery was the greatest killer on the Western Front, responsible for 58% of all wounds and massive compound fractures deeply contaminated by Flemish mud. **Hinge Question:** Why did high explosive artillery shrapnel create far more dangerous and infectious wounds than rifle bullets?",
