          "caption": "Clinical radiograph demonstrating metallic bullet localisation within the cranium of a living soldier using a lead-wire localisation cage (Professor Waymouth Reid's case, RAMC, c.1916). Cross-hairs and coordinate grids allowed surgeons to calculate the precise depth of intracranial projectiles before performing trephining or craniotomy.",
