          "content": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[2.1]</span> Wounded men were evacuated next to the **Advanced Dressing Station (ADS)**, located roughly 1,000 to 2,000 yards behind the frontline in ruined farmhouses or tents. Run by the RAMC Field Ambulance unit, it staffed up to ten medical officers.<br><br><span class=\"para-ref\">[2.2]</span> The ADS performed wound redressing, shock treatment with warm blankets, and splinting. In massive offensives, Dressing Stations treated hundreds of casualties per hour. However, like the RAP, Dressing Stations were not surgical hospitals; their sole purpose was stabilizing wounded soldiers for transport to the Casualty Clearing Station.",
