              "model_answer": "Source C depicts an exhausted RAMC stretcher bearer trudging through mud with bowed head and hollow eyes while carrying a heavily bandaged, unconscious casualty on his back under a storm-swept sky. From this, it can be inferred that stretcher bearers faced immense physical strain, prolonged sleep deprivation, and acute psychological trauma as they navigated devastated battlefields under fire, bearing sole responsibility for rescuing mangled comrades from No Man's Land.",
