          "content": "<span class=\"para-ref\">[4.1]</span> Following surgery at the CCS, stabilized patients were loaded onto ambulance trains and transported to vast **Base Hospitals** on the French coast, centered around ports like Boulogne, Le Tréport, and Étaples.<br><br><span class=\"para-ref\">[4.2]</span> Base Hospitals operated thousands of beds in converted hotels, villas, or large tent complexes. They provided specialized medical care: dividing wards into specialized units for brain trauma, fractured bones, and plastic reconstruction. Convalescing soldiers were rehabilitated or evacuated back to Britain (\"Blighty\") on hospital ships for long-term recovery.",
