              "question": "How does Source E corroborate the role of the Advanced Dressing Station within the wider chain of evacuation?",
              "model_answer": "Source E corroborates historical knowledge that Advanced Dressing Stations acted as vital operational links between the trenches and rearward hospitals. By demonstrating how 2,400 casualties were triaged, treated for shock with warmth and fluids, and rapidly dispatched by motor ambulance within six hours to Casualty Clearing Stations, the report confirms that ADS facilities focused on stabilizing casualties and expediting surgical transfer rather than holding patients for prolonged treatment.",
